---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ROUTES } from '../../i18n/config.ts';
---

<Base route="privacy" title="Privacy policy – KNOX">
  <main id="main" class="section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <p class="eyebrow">KNOX – The Musical</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>

      <p>
        This is a courtesy translation. Only the German version
        (<a href={ROUTES.privacy.de} hreflang="de" lang="de">Datenschutzerklärung</a>) is legally
        binding.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>
        The controller within the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:<br />
        Christian Peters<br />
        Wollankstraße 108<br />
        13187 Berlin<br />
        Germany<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:kontakt@knox-das-musical.de">kontakt@knox-das-musical.de</a>
      </p>

      <h2>2. General information on data processing</h2>
      <p>
        This website is a purely informational site about the musical KNOX. We process personal
        data only to the extent technically necessary. This website uses <strong>no cookies</strong>
        (for the locally stored language choice, see section&nbsp;6), <strong>no analytics or
        tracking services</strong> and embeds <strong>no content from third-party servers</strong>.
        All fonts are loaded locally from our server; in particular, no connection to Google Fonts
        is made. The website is transmitted in encrypted form via TLS (HTTPS).
      </p>

      <h2>3. Hosting and server log files</h2>
      <p>
        When you visit this website, our hosting provider's server automatically processes
        information that your browser transmits (so-called server log files): IP address, date and
        time of access, requested file, amount of data transferred, browser type and version, and
        operating system. This data is technically necessary to provide the website securely and
        reliably; the legal basis is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest). This data is not
        merged with other data sources or analysed for marketing purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The website is hosted by Vercel Inc., 440 N Barranca Ave #4133, Covina, CA 91723, USA.
        Where personal data is transferred to the USA in the process, this is done on the basis of
        a data processing agreement and the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses or
        the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. Further information:
        <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Vercel's
        privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Contacting us by email</h2>
      <p>
        If you contact us by email, we process the data you provide (email address, content of
        your message) solely to handle your enquiry. The legal basis is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(b) GDPR
        where your enquiry is aimed at concluding a contract, and otherwise Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR.
        We delete the data as soon as it is no longer required to handle your enquiry and no
        statutory retention obligations apply.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Links to YouTube</h2>
      <p>
        On this website we link to videos on YouTube. These are simple external links – loading
        our website <strong>does not transfer any data to YouTube or Google</strong>. Only when you
        click a link do you leave our website; from that point on,
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google's
        privacy policy</a> applies.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Language selection</h2>
      <p>
        This website is available in German and English. On your first visit to the homepage, a
        script selects the appropriate language version based on your browser's language setting.
        This check takes place exclusively in your browser; no data is transmitted to us or stored
        in the process.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you change the language yourself using the language switch, this choice (“de” or “en”)
        is saved in your browser's local storage so that the language you chose is shown again on
        your next visit. This information never leaves your device. The storage is strictly
        necessary for the function you explicitly requested (Section&nbsp;25(2) no.&nbsp;2 of the
        German Telecommunications Digital Services Data Protection Act, TDDDG). You can remove it at
        any time by clearing the stored website data in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the following rights vis-à-vis the controller with regard to your personal data:
        access (Art.&nbsp;15 GDPR), rectification (Art.&nbsp;16 GDPR), erasure (Art.&nbsp;17 GDPR),
        restriction of processing (Art.&nbsp;18 GDPR), data portability (Art.&nbsp;20 GDPR) and
        objection to processing (Art.&nbsp;21 GDPR).
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority
        (Art.&nbsp;77 GDPR). The competent authority for Berlin is the Berlin Commissioner for Data
        Protection and Freedom of Information (Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und
        Informationsfreiheit), Alt-Moabit 59–61, 10555 Berlin.
      </p>

      <p>Last updated: November 2026</p>

      <p class="back">
        <a href={ROUTES.legalNotice.en}>Legal notice</a> · <a href={ROUTES.home.en}>← Back to the homepage</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
